{
  "id": "kubernetes_node_and_rollout_totals",
  "title": "Node association totals, unattributed series survival, and old/new rollout attribution equal the hand-authored Kubernetes results",
  "obligations": [
    "fixed-case-12",
    "fixed-case-9",
    "gap-k8s-acquisition",
    "invariant-10",
    "invariant-11",
    "invariant-13",
    "route-promql-info"
  ],
  "routes": [
    "columnar"
  ],
  "open_decisions": [
    "4",
    "1"
  ],
  "scope": "Settled enrichment arithmetic only: node A carries 100 + 200 MiB = 300 MiB, an unassociated 50 MiB series survives an unfiltered aggregation (100 + 200 + 50 = 350 MiB), an explicit node filter selects only matching series, and a rollout with two distinct owners counts old 0.2 + new 0.3 = 0.5 exactly once each. It does not decide how a plain scrape acquires a collection-time association (decision 4) or how same-name/different-UID objects are identified without an explicit distinguishing identifying attribute (decision 1): the two rollout Resources state distinct service.instance.id values, which is a compatibility stand-in, not an Entity-aware identity rule. 100, 200 and 50 MiB are exact binary multiples; 0.2 + 0.3 is exactly 0.5 in IEEE-754, and a candidate that returns 0.5000000000000001 fails.",
